\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Use the linear substitution $u=13 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=13,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{13})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\n\n$$\n|u|=|13 x|=13|x|,\\qquad \\frac{1}{|x|}=\\frac{13}{|u|}.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{13}{|13 x|\\sqrt{(13 x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 13\\int \\frac{1}{|13 x|\\sqrt{(13 x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 13(\\frac{1}{13})\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 1\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}+C \\\\  &= \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(13 x \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|13 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f28e42b-8620-5ae1-8f04-805f88867c6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676881} {:answer/id #uuid "228bf48b-6c00-5de6-bd83-cd4703885c3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676897} {:answer/id #uuid "75d06d6f-6fe5-5d6f-9007-78758ffc948c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676947} {:answer/id #uuid "bc16c7b4-f2db-5f7c-a2ff-83546ce380d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676998} {:answer/id #uuid "f3779970-0bfa-5296-b548-2b234032333d" 